    "q-51492": {
      "dom_id": "step-q51492",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Solve the equation $\\frac{5}{4x+24}=\\frac{5}{x+6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that $x=-6$ cannot be a solution since division by $0$ is undefined. \n\nTo solve the equation, we first apply cross-multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{4x+24} & =\\frac{5}{x+6} \\\\ 5\\cdot (x+6) & =(4x+24)\\cdot 5 \\\\ 5x+30 & =20x+120\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the addition and multiplication principles, as usual:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+30 & =20x+120 \\\\ 5x+30-5x & =20x+120-5x \\\\ 30 & =15x+120 \\\\ 30-120 & =15x+120-120 \\\\ -90 & =15x \\\\ \\frac{-90}{15} & =\\frac{15x}{15} \\\\ -6 & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x=-6$ cannot be a solution, the equation has no solutions.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
